// The four ordered-sequence questions route through the same first-argument dispatch as the rest,
// so a Set is refused with the shared message rather than falling through to "unknown function".
// What *cannot* be checked here is the thing three of them actually require: that the sequence is
// already in order. That precondition is the caller's in either world, and `is_sorted` is the
// function for asking it.
fn main() {
    print(lower_bound(Set<int> { 1, 2 }, 1))
}
